{
  "artifact": "mindmake-approved-production-routes-r24",
  "recordedAt": "2026-09-24",
  "status": "candidate record. Owner approval for this revision is NOT recorded. Do not treat it as an approval.",
  "scopeRequested": "One instruction about /new-age-leadership, raised from live mindmake.co: the page was supposed to build as it is scrolled and instead needed its buttons pressed, it showed large empty bands, and its top bar was not the one every other page wears. The cause of the first two was the same: the prototype's body-level overflow-x:hidden, scoped onto .nal-page, made that div its own scrollport, so every position:sticky on the route pinned to a container that never scrolls. All three pinned sequences scrolled away after one screen and left the rest of their tracks empty. Fixed at the cause, given the same scroll-built history on a phone that the desktop had, turned the one timed carousel into a sequence the reader drives, and put the route inside the shared shell. No approved word changed, no new claim, price, section or route.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "Fix the scoping fault rather than the symptom. overflow-x:clip clips the same overflow without creating a scroll container, so the composition is unchanged and every pin the prototype designed starts working.",
    "The film pause moves into the hero rather than floating. Measured at 1440 and 390 across the whole scroll, all four screen corners are occupied by this composition at some position, so a standing control would overlap a heading, an era button, the range input, the benefit arrows or the privacy notice. The operating system's reduced-motion setting remains the path for anyone who needs motion stopped everywhere.",
    "The six AI Brain benefits stop advancing on a timer. On a page whose argument is carried by scrolling, a 6.2-second carousel was the one element that moved on its own and changed the sentence under whoever was reading it.",
    "The phone keeps the era buttons and the range input. They are the assistive and reduced-motion path through the same four states; they now move the page to a state rather than swapping it underneath a reader who has not moved.",
    "The gate proves states by scrolling and never by clicking, forwards and in reverse, and carries a negative control that removes the pins. The old gate clicked every control and passed a page where nothing pinned at all."
  ],
